  "round": 1,
  "prompt": "What is the VAT treatment of the sale of a residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe sale of a residential lot valued at ₱1.9 million is subject to VAT because it exceeds the threshold of ₱1.5 million for residential lots, as stipulated in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC) and its implementing regulations.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\n- **RR 16-2005**: Implements the VAT provisions and specifies that sales of residential lots exceeding ₱1.5 million are subject to VAT.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor the seller, this means that they must charge VAT on the sale of the residential lot, which will be at the standard rate of 12% on the gross selling price. The seller is responsible for remitting this VAT to the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR). Buyers should be aware that the total cost of purchasing the lot will include this VAT, impacting their overall financial planning for the acquisition.",
